## Dawn, then nothing

::bg{location="hearth" time="dawn"}
::music{action="start" mood="elegy" volume="down"}
@narrator{code="0010"}: She had seen the sky. Then the sky had folded up like a letter, and she was here.
::use{component="hearthFire" flare="high"}
::auto{character="maud" anchor="center" action="fadeInUp"}
@maud{code="0010" emotion="stricken"}: You got out. You actually — I felt the fire jump. It hasn't done that in forty years.
@wren{code="0010"}: It didn't hold. I was out, and then I wasn't.
@maud{code="0020" emotion="warm"}: It never holds the first time. But it knows your name now. That's how it starts.
::set{user.bond.maud += 1}
